<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION INCHES UP.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION INCHES UP.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse rose to 5.255 billion litas last week from 5.218</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					    June 09-13     June 02-06</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		  14,436	   15,235</p>
<p>    Executed orders		   1,276	    1,053</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)	     932		911</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL     2,094,280	2,476,680</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		 124		71</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	   7,427,650	2,088,100</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week     61,255,197     60,154,585</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week     3,012,449	3,312,849</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	   2,089,500	2,437,150</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	   6,938,780	2,088,100</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	   3		  6</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	 493,640	  39,530</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
